Carafe Lab: when a game stops, Eden hands memory back to the system: the pages of the emulated Switch's memory that
the stopped game touched, and the heap that Eden's own threads freed. The Switch's memory stays reserved for the next
game, so one Eden can run game after game without running out of memory. Linux only.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

